{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Remember what Amalek did to you</b>. I have already cited (Ramban on Deuteronomy 24:9) the midrash that they expounded regarding this in the Sifra (Bechukotai, parasha 1:3): \"One might think in your heart — when it says <i>lo tishkaḥ</i> ('you shall not forget'), behold, forgetting of the heart is stated; so what do I fulfill with <i>zakhor</i> ('remember')? That you should recite it with your mouth.\" And likewise in the Sifrei (Tetzeh 166): \"<i>Zakhor et asher asah lekha Amalek</i> — with the mouth; <i>lo tishkaḥ</i> — in the heart.\" And I do not know what this oral remembrance is: whether it means that the passage of Amalek is read in public, and we thereby learn from the Torah the reading of the <i>zakhor</i> portion on the second (reading of the Megillah, see Megillah 29a), and it would serve as scriptural support for the reading of the Megillah from the Torah. And the correct view in my eyes is that it means we must not forget what Amalek did to us until we blot out his name from under the heavens, and we shall recount this to our children and to our generations, saying to them: thus did the wicked one do to us, and for this reason we were commanded to blot out his name. And similarly regarding the matter of Miriam, we were commanded to make it known to our children and to recount it to generations, and even though it would have been fitting also to conceal it so as not to speak of the disgrace of the righteous, nevertheless Scripture commanded to make it known and to reveal it, so that a warning against evil speech be placed in their mouths, because it is a great sin and causes many evils, and people stumble in it constantly, as they said (Bava Batra 165a), and all are in the dust of evil speech:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The parenthetical reference to Megillah 29 is resolved as Megillah 29a. The phrase הזכיר בשניה refers to the practice of reading the zakhor passage, which the Talmud links to the obligation to read the Megillah; the translation preserves the ellipsis in Ramban's compressed reference."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:55:51.621088750Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}